<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan raises August bunker prices by $5/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan raises August bunker prices by $5/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has raised its bunker fuel prices by $5.00 per tonne effective August 14, a company statement said on Friday.</p>
<p>Posted prices for 180, 280 and 380-centistoke bunker fuel delivered at the ports of Keelung, Hualien, Taichung and Suao were raised by $5.00 to $124.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>Term prices were also raised by $5.00 to $121.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>CPC is Taiwan's monopoly supplier of bunker fuels.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703571)</p>
</text>
